mode: "100644"
text: "# The NORTH framework — turn wishes into a measurable cascade\n\nMost social \"goals\" are wishes — \"grow our following,\" \"go viral,\" \"do better.\" NORTH turns them into a\ncascade you can manage: anchored to the business, one clear North Star per channel, SMART, benchmarked,\nand capped for focus. (Setting targets is this skill; **measuring** them is `analytics-and-reporting`.)\n\n## N — Name the business goal\n- Anchor every social goal to a **real business outcome** (awareness / leads / sales / retention / care).\n- If a metric doesn't **ladder up** to that outcome, it's vanity — cut it. Pull the outcome from\n  `social-strategy`.\n\n## O — One North Star per channel\n- Pick **one North Star metric per channel**, tied to its **win condition**: awareness-first → reach;\n  consideration-first → CTR/clicks; conversion-first → CVR/CPA.\n- Add **1–2 supporting metrics** per North Star (diagnostics), not ten.\n\n## R — Render it SMART\n- Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, Time-bound — **a number + a deadline + a method.**\n- \"Grow newsletter sign-ups from social 200 → 300/mo by Q3 via Story link stickers\" — not \"get more clicks.\"\n\n## T — Target from benchmarks\n- Set the number from a **benchmark**: your own **baseline** (extrapolate past performance) or comparable\n  accounts — **achievable yet ambitious.** No baseline → set a **learning goal** first (don't invent one).\n- Use **leading + lagging** indicators; only commit to KPIs the team can **actually influence**.\n\n## H — Hold to 3–5 + set triggers\n- Cap at **3–5 KPIs / objectives** for focus. Set **action thresholds** (\"if X holds but Y drops → do Z\").\n- **Review** weekly (metrics) / monthly (tactics) / quarterly (the goals themselves); **miss → pivot\n  tactics before moving the goal.** Hand the targets to **analytics-and-reporting** to measure.\n\n## The goals brief a request should fill\n```\nBUSINESS GOAL: the outcome this ladders up to (from social-strategy)\nOBJECTIVE (SMART): number + deadline + method\nNORTH STAR (per channel): the one win-condition metric + 1–2 supporting\nTARGET: from baseline/benchmark — achievable yet ambitious (or a learning goal if no data)\nGUARDRAIL: the quality floor that prevents gaming (e.g. ER while growing followers)\nTRIGGERS + CADENCE: thresholds that force a choice; weekly/monthly/quarterly review\nHANDOFF: measured by analytics-and-reporting\n```\n"
